ve)\n    selectors_cube: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    public_values: &'a DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_3bs: &'a [EF],                               // Per-interaction eq_3b weights\n    cached_mains: &'a [CommittedTraceData<...>],\n    common_main: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    eq_xis: &'a FxHashMap<usize, EqEvalLayers<EF>>,\n    d_lambda_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    beta_pows: &'a [EF],\n    l_skip: usize,                                  // Skip domain exponent\n    constraint_degree: usize,\n    xi: &'a [EF],\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,                          // Per-thread memory limit\n}\n```\n\n### process_air_round0 Function\n**Location:** Lines 140-272\n\n**Core Processing Pipeline:**\n\n1. **Setup** (lines 143-162):\n   - Extract symbolic constraints from single AIR\n   - Create array of trace pointers (cached_mains + common_main)\n   - Copy to device\n\n2. **Zerocheck Constraints** (lines 164-211):\n   - Calculate num_cosets_zc = constraint_degree - 1\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()`\n   - Convert output evaluations to polynomial via IDFT\n   - Compute polynomial coefficients using sumcheck formula\n   - Store as Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>\n\n3. **Logup Interactions** (lines 213-263):\n   - Calculate num_cosets_logup = constraint_degree (no -1)\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()`\n   - Extract (numer, denom) from Frac<EF> evaluations\n   - Apply normalization if n is negative\n   - Convert evaluations to polynomials via IDFT\n   - Store as Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>> pairs\n\n4. **Return** (lines 266-271):\n   - Return `Round0AirResult` with all three optional polynomials\n\n### sumcheck_uni_round0_polys Function\n**Location:** Lines 766-983 (the Round 0 orchestration function)\n\n**Phase 1: Work Item Creation** (lines 900-926)\n\n```rust\nlet per_thread_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.max(1);\n\nlet mut work_items: Vec<Round0AirWorkItem<HS>> = izip!(\n    &ctx.per_trace,\n    &self.n_per_trace,\n    &selectors_base,\n    &self.public_values_per_trace,\n    &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n)\n.enumerate()\n.map(|(trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, sel, pv, eq3b))| {\n    Round0AirWorkItem {\n        trace_idx,\n        single_pk: &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx],\n        n,\n        selectors_cube: sel,\n        public_values: pv,\n        eq_3bs: eq3b,\n        cached_mains: &air_ctx.cached_mains,\n        common_main: &air_ctx.common_main,\n        eq_xis: &self.eq_xis,\n        d_lambda_pows,\n        beta_pows: &self.beta_pows,\n        l_skip,\n        constraint_degree: self.constraint_degree,\n        xi: &self.xi,\n        max_temp_bytes: per_thread_temp_bytes,\n    }\n})\n.collect();\n\n// Sort by descending height for better load balance\nwork_items.sort_by(|a, b| b.common_main.height().cmp(&a.common_main.height()));\n```\n\n**Key:** Work items are sorted by descending trace height for load balancing across thread chunks.\n\n**Phase 2: Parallel Processing** (lines 944-966)\n\n```rust\nlet num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n} else {\n    1\n};\n\nlet results: Vec<Round0AirResult> = if num_threads <= 1 {\n    work_items\n        .iter()\n        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?\n} else {\n    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = work_items\n            .chunks(chunk_size)\n            .map(|chunk| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n                    chunk.iter().map(|w| process_air_round0(w)).collect()\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        // Collect from all threads...\n    })?\n};\n```\n\n**Decision Logic:**\n- Single-threaded if < 100 AIRs\n- Multi-threaded if >= 100 AIRs, capped at NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS (8)\n- Each thread processes a chunk of work items sequentially\n\n**Phase 3: Result Scattering** (lines 969-979)\n\n```rust\nlet mut batch_sp_poly = vec![UnivariatePoly::new(vec![]); 3 * num_present_airs];\n\nfor result in results {\n    if let Some(poly) = result.zerocheck_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_numer_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_denom_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx + 1] = poly;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Storage Pattern:**\n- Indices 0..2*num_present_airs: logup polynomials (2 per AIR: numer, denom)\n- Indices 2*num_present_airs..3*num_present_airs: zerocheck polynomials (1 per AIR)\n\n---\n\n## 5. **Key Data Flow and Computation Patterns**\n\n### Constraint Evaluation Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Source | Round0 Zerocheck | Round0 Logup |\n|-----------|--------|------------------|--------------|\n| skip_domain | l_skip | 1 << l_skip | 1 << l_skip |\n| num_x | n_lift | 1 << n_lift | 1 << n_lift |\n| num_cosets | constraint_degree | deg - 1 | deg |\n| Output size | skip_domain * num_cosets | (1 << l_skip) * (deg-1) | (1 << l_skip) * deg |\n\n### Per-AIR Kernel Launch Pattern (Current)\n\n```\nFor each AIR (sequentially within thread chunk):\n  1. Allocate intermediates buffer\n  2. Allocate temp_sums buffer\n  3. Launch zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints kernel\n  4. Launch logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0 kernel\n  5. Copy outputs to host\n  6. Compute polynomial coefficients (CPU IDFT)\n  7. Free GPU buffers (async)\n```\n\n### Memory Management\n\n- **Intermediate buffer:** Holds DAG node evaluations buffered per row\n  - Size depends on: buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes\n  - Calculated via FFI: `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(...)`\n\n- **Temp sums buffer:** Accumulates polynomial evaluations\n  - For zerocheck: type EF, size calculated via FFI\n  - For logup: type Frac<EF> (2x the size of EF)\n\n- **Per-thread limit:** `memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS`\n  - Allows kernels to allocate adaptively within constraints\n  - Warning logged if actual usage exceeds limit\n\n### Batching Opportunities for Descriptor-Array Implementation\n\n1. **Pre-batching Step:** Group AIRs by compatible parameters\n   - Same constraint_degree → same num_cosets\n   - Same n → same skip_domain, num_x\n   - Batch construction in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` Phase 1\n\n2. **Kernel Launch Pattern:**\n   - Create batch descriptors for all AIRs in each group\n   - Single kernel launch processes all descriptors\n   - Each CUDA block handles one AIR's evaluation\n\n3. **Memory Model:**\n   - Shared intermediates buffer for entire batch (or per-descriptor base pointers)\n   - Shared rules/used_nodes with per-descriptor rule offsets\n   - Per-descriptor output pointers in batch descriptor\n\n4. **Result Collection:**\n   - Batch kernel writes outputs directly to batched buffers\n   - No scatter/gather phase needed\n   - Reduced GPU-CPU synchronization points\n\n---\n\n## 6. **Critical Implementation Details**\n\n### Buffer Size Calculation Philosophy\n\nThe FFI functions return buffer capacities based on:\n- `buffer_size`: DAG nodes needing per-row buffering\n- `skip_domain`, `num_x`, `num_cosets`: Domain size factors\n- `max_temp_bytes`: Maximum allowable GPU memory\n\nThe kernel adapts allocation strategy based on available memory. Allocating more than requested is acceptable (warning only), as kernels handle overallocation gracefully.\n\n### Lambda Powers and Constraints\n\n- `lambda_pows` for zerocheck: powers of lambda for constraint linear combinations\n  - Length = max_num_constraints per AIR\n  - Precomputed before Round 0 phase\n\n- `beta_pows` for logup: powers of beta parameter\n  - Length = max_interaction_length + 1\n  - Shared across all logup evaluations\n\n### Eq_3b Weights (Logup-Specific)\n\n- Computed per AIR based on interaction properties\n- Stored as `eq_3b_per_trace` (Vec<Vec<EF>>)\n- Converted to numer_weights and denom_weights per interaction\n- Weights accumulate when expression nodes are shared\n\n### Polynomial Construction from Evaluations\n\n**Zerocheck:**\n```\n1. Evaluate on cosets indexed by (coset_idx, skip_domain_idx)\n2. Transpose to column-major: values[skip_domain_idx * num_cosets + coset_idx]\n3. IDFT with omega_root (generator of domain)\n4. Compute polynomial coefficients: c_i = -q_i + (i >= skip_domain ? q_{i-skip_domain} : 0)\n```\n\n**Logup:**\n```\n1. Extract (numer, denom) from Frac<EF>\n2. Apply normalization if n < 0\n3. Transpose evaluations\n4. Two IDFTs (numerator and denominator)\n5. Return as separate polynomials\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. **Batching Implementation Recommendations**\n\n### Descriptor Structure\n```rust\npub struct Round0Descriptor {\n    pub air_idx: u32,\n    pub trace_idx: u32,\n    pub n: isize,\n    pub constraint_degree: u32,\n    pub num_cosets: u32,\n    pub skip_domain: u32,\n    pub num_x: u32,\n    pub height: u32,\n    pub output_offset_zc: u32,\n    pub output_offset_logup: u32,\n    pub rules_offset: u32,\n    pub numer_weights_offset: u32,\n    pub denom_weights_offset: u32,\n    // Pointers to shared per-batch data\n}\n```\n\n### Batched Kernel Interface\n```rust\nfn _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched(\n    descriptors: *const Round0Descriptor,\n    num_descriptors: u32,\n    // Shared buffers\n    tmp_sums_buffer: *mut EF,\n    output: *mut EF,\n    selectors_cubes: *const *const F,  // Array of selectors per descriptor\n    // ... other shared inputs\n) -> i32;\n```\n\n### Memory Layout Strategy\n- Allocate single large intermediate buffer with per-descriptor offsets\n- Allocate single large output buffer indexed by descriptor output_offsets\n- Rules and weights concatenated with per-descriptor base offsets\n- Reduces allocation overhead and improves cache locality\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive analysis provides the foundation for understanding how to batch the per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches into descriptor-array based batched kernels."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3eab5b9b-40e0-4e43-bd71-fd448feabe6e","uuid":"7b981fe7-0652-4226-adf2-8bf22b0adbf0","timestamp":"2026-04-13T13:13:31.843Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the following files in the stark-backend repo at /home/georg/stark-backend and provide a comprehensive summary of each. I need to understand the current Round 0 implementation to batch per-AIR kernel launches into descriptor-array batched kernels.\n\nRead these files in their entirety:\n1. `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` — focus on lines 850-1000 (the Round 0 section)\n2. `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` — the full file\n3. `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` — especially the FFI bindings for round0 functions\n4. `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs` — the AirDataGpu struct and keygen\n\nFor each file, report:\n- Key structs and their fields\n- Key functions and their signatures\n- The flow of the Round 0 per-AIR processing\n- Any existing batched patterns I can follow\n- Important constants and thresholds\n\nBe thorough — I need enough detail to implement the batched version.","agentId":"a7a28592af818407a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive summary document:\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: Round 0 Implementation in stark-backend\n\n### Overview\nThe Round 0 implementation in stark-backend processes per-AIR kernel launches sequentially using OS threads and CUDA streams. The current architecture orchestrates independent AIR constraint evaluations in parallel across multiple threads, each managing its own CUDA stream and temporary GPU memory.\n\n---\n\n## 1. **pkey.rs** - Key Structures and Data Organization\n\n### `AirDataGpu` Struct\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs:24-32`\n\n```rust\npub struct AirDataGpu {\n    pub interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules,\n    pub zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>,  // BUFFER_VARS=true\n    pub zerocheck_mle: ConstraintOnlyRules<false>,\n    pub zerocheck_monomials: Option<ZerocheckMonomials>,\n    pub interaction_monomials: Option<InteractionMonomials>,\n}\n```\n\n**Key Properties:**\n- Per-AIR data prepared and stored in GPU proving keys\n- `zerocheck_round0` uses buffered variable evaluation (BUFFER_VARS=true)\n- Rules are precomputed and encoded for GPU execution\n\n### `EvalRules` Struct (Core Rule Container)\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs:50-55`\n\n```rust\npub struct EvalRules {\n    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>,      // Encoded rule expressions\n    pub d_used_nodes: DeviceBuffer<usize>, // DAG node indices used\n    pub buffer_size: u32,                  // \"How many DAG nodes per row need buffering\"\n}\n```\n\n**Critical:** `buffer_size` is NOT the capacity - it's a multiplier for runtime-calculated intermediate buffer capacity.\n\n### `InteractionEvalRules` Struct\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs:35-43`\n\n```rust\npub struct InteractionEvalRules {\n    pub(crate) inner: EvalRules,\n    pub(crate) d_pair_idxs: DeviceBuffer<u32>,  // Maps constraint idx back to unsorted (numer, denom) pairs\n    pub(crate) max_fields_len: usize,            // Max message length across all interactions\n}\n```\n\n**Constraint Expression:** `constraint_idx => 2 * interaction_idx + is_denom`\n\n### Construction (`AirDataGpu::new`)\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs:86-116`\n\nFor each AIR:\n1. Extract symbolic constraints from vk\n2. Create `InteractionEvalRules::new()` for logup interactions\n3. Create `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new()` for zerocheck Round 0\n4. Build optional monomials structures for both zerocheck and logup\n\n---\n\n## 2. **round0.rs** - Per-AIR Evaluation Functions\n\n### `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` (Plain AIR constraints)\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:31-124`\n\n**Signature:**\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,        // Array of pointers to trace data\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,                         // Hypercube evaluations\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    skip_domain: u32,                           // 1 << l_skip\n    num_x: u32,                                 // 1 << n_lift\n    height: u32,                                // Trace height\n    num_cosets: u32,                            // constraint_degree - 1\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError>\n```\n\n**Processing Flow:**\n1. Check if constraints exist; return empty buffer if none\n2. Query intermediate buffer size via FFI: `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(...)`\n3. Query temp sums buffer size via FFI: `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(...)`\n4. Allocate intermediates and temp_sums buffers\n5. Call `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` kernel\n6. Return output buffer (sp_evals)\n\n**Key Parameters:**\n- `num_cosets = constraint_degree - 1` (evaluating quotient polynomial)\n- Preprocessed data is optional (null if none exists)\n- `eq_cube` must have at least `num_x` elements representing hypercube evaluations\n\n### `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (Logup interactions)\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs:132-275`\n\n**Signature:**\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    beta_pows: &[EF],\n    eq_3bs: &[EF],                             // Per-interaction weights\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,                           // constraint_degree (not -1)\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError>\n```\n\n**Processing Flow:**\n1. Return empty buffer if no interactions (eq_3bs.is_empty())\n2. Build a new \"interactions DAG\":\n   - Create per-rule weights by iterating through all interactions\n   - Weight each (count, message[0..]) expression by eq_3b values\n   - Deduplicate DAG indices\n3. Query buffer sizes for logup (same FFI pattern as zerocheck)\n4. Allocate intermediates and temp_sums buffers\n5. Call `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` kernel\n6. Return output buffer (s_evals of type `Frac<EF>`)\n\n**Critical Difference from Zerocheck:**\n- `num_cosets_logup = constraint_degree` (not -1)\n- Output is fractional (numerator/denominator pairs)\n- Weights are precomputed per-rule based on interaction indices\n\n### Weight Computation in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n**Location:** Lines 161-207\n\n```rust\nlet mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\nlet mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\nlet mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n\nfor (interaction_idx, interaction) in symbolic.interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n    let count_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(&interaction.count as *)];\n    let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n    numer_weights[count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n    denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[interaction.message.len()] \n                    * F::from_u32(interaction.bus_index as u32 + 1);\n\n    for (message_idx, message) in interaction.message.iter().enumerate() {\n        let message_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(message as *)];\n        let message_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&message_dag_idx];\n        denom_weights[message_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key Insight:** Expression nodes shared across multiple interactions accumulate weights across all occurrences.\n\n---\n\n## 3. **logup_zerocheck.rs** - FFI Bindings and Wrappers\n\n### Round 0 FFI Functions\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:294-373`\n\n#### Zerocheck Kernel\n```rust\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints(\n        tmp_sums_buffer: *mut EF,\n        output: *mut EF,\n        selectors_cube: *const F,\n        preprocessed: *const F,\n        main_parts: *const *const F,      // Array of trace pointers\n        eq_cube: *const EF,\n        d_lambda_pows: *const EF,\n        public_values: *const F,\n        d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void, // Encoded rules\n        rules_len: usize,\n        d_used_nodes: *const usize,       // DAG node indices\n        used_nodes_len: usize,\n        lambda_len: usize,                // Unused but part of signature\n        buffer_size: u32,\n        d_intermediates: *mut F,\n        skip_domain: u32,\n        num_x: u32,\n        height: u32,\n        num_cosets: u32,\n        g_shift: F,\n        max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n```\n\n#### Buffer Size Queries\n```rust\npub fn _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n    buffer_size: u32,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> usize;\n\npub fn _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n    buffer_size: u32,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> usize;\n```\n\n#### Logup Kernel\n```rust\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn _logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(\n        tmp_sums_buffer: *mut Frac<EF>,\n        output: *mut Frac<EF>,           // Currently unused (only tmp_sums written)\n        selectors_cube: *const F,\n        preprocessed: *const F,\n        main_parts: *const *const F,\n        eq_cube: *const EF,\n        public_values: *const F,\n        numer_weights: *const EF,        // Per-rule weights for numerator\n        denom_weights: *const EF,        // Per-rule weights for denominator\n        denom_sum_init: EF,              // Initial denominator sum value\n        d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n        rules_len: usize,\n        buffer_size: u32,\n        d_intermediates: *mut F,\n        skip_domain: u32,\n        num_x: u32,\n        height: u32,\n        num_cosets: u32,\n        g_shift: F,\n        max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    ) -> i32;\n}\n```\n\n### Safe Wrapper Functions\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:962-1050`\n\n```rust\npub unsafe fn zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints(\n    tmp_sums_buffer: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    preprocessed: *const F,\n    main_ptrs: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    rules: &DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n    used_nodes: &DeviceBuffer<usize>,\n    buffer_size: u32,\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError>\n\npub unsafe fn logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(\n    tmp_sums_buffer: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    preprocessed: *const F,\n    main_ptrs: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    numer_weights: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    denom_weights: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    denom_sum_init: EF,\n    rules: &DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n    buffer_size: u32,\n    intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError>\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. **mod.rs** - Round 0 Orchestration and Parallelization\n\n### Constants\n**Location:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:95, 101`\n\n```rust\nconst NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS: usize = 8;                // OS threads for parallel Round 0 processing\nconst DAG_FALLBACK_MONOMIAL_RATIO: usize = 2;      // Threshold for monomial vs DAG evaluation\n```\n\n### Round0AirResult Struct\n**Location:** Lines 114-119\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirResult {\n    trace_idx: usize,\n    zerocheck_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,    // Plain constraint evaluation\n    logup_numer_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,  // Interaction numerator\n    logup_denom_poly: Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>,  // Interaction denominator\n}\n```\n\n### Round0AirWorkItem Struct\n**Location:** Lines 122-138\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    trace_idx: usize,\n    single_pk: &'a DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    n: isize,                                        // Lift exponent (can be negative)\n    selectors_cube: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    public_values: &'a DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_3bs: &'a [EF],                               // Per-interaction eq_3b weights\n    cached_mains: &'a [CommittedTraceData<...>],\n    common_main: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    eq_xis: &'a FxHashMap<usize, EqEvalLayers<EF>>,\n    d_lambda_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    beta_pows: &'a [EF],\n    l_skip: usize,                                  // Skip domain exponent\n    constraint_degree: usize,\n    xi: &'a [EF],\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,                          // Per-thread memory limit\n}\n```\n\n### process_air_round0 Function\n**Location:** Lines 140-272\n\n**Core Processing Pipeline:**\n\n1. **Setup** (lines 143-162):\n   - Extract symbolic constraints from single AIR\n   - Create array of trace pointers (cached_mains + common_main)\n   - Copy to device\n\n2. **Zerocheck Constraints** (lines 164-211):\n   - Calculate num_cosets_zc = constraint_degree - 1\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()`\n   - Convert output evaluations to polynomial via IDFT\n   - Compute polynomial coefficients using sumcheck formula\n   - Store as Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>>\n\n3. **Logup Interactions** (lines 213-263):\n   - Calculate num_cosets_logup = constraint_degree (no -1)\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()`\n   - Extract (numer, denom) from Frac<EF> evaluations\n   - Apply normalization if n is negative\n   - Convert evaluations to polynomials via IDFT\n   - Store as Option<UnivariatePoly<EF>> pairs\n\n4. **Return** (lines 266-271):\n   - Return `Round0AirResult` with all three optional polynomials\n\n### sumcheck_uni_round0_polys Function\n**Location:** Lines 766-983 (the Round 0 orchestration function)\n\n**Phase 1: Work Item Creation** (lines 900-926)\n\n```rust\nlet per_thread_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.max(1);\n\nlet mut work_items: Vec<Round0AirWorkItem<HS>> = izip!(\n    &ctx.per_trace,\n    &self.n_per_trace,\n    &selectors_base,\n    &self.public_values_per_trace,\n    &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n)\n.enumerate()\n.map(|(trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, sel, pv, eq3b))| {\n    Round0AirWorkItem {\n        trace_idx,\n        single_pk: &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx],\n        n,\n        selectors_cube: sel,\n        public_values: pv,\n        eq_3bs: eq3b,\n        cached_mains: &air_ctx.cached_mains,\n        common_main: &air_ctx.common_main,\n        eq_xis: &self.eq_xis,\n        d_lambda_pows,\n        beta_pows: &self.beta_pows,\n        l_skip,\n        constraint_degree: self.constraint_degree,\n        xi: &self.xi,\n        max_temp_bytes: per_thread_temp_bytes,\n    }\n})\n.collect();\n\n// Sort by descending height for better load balance\nwork_items.sort_by(|a, b| b.common_main.height().cmp(&a.common_main.height()));\n```\n\n**Key:** Work items are sorted by descending trace height for load balancing across thread chunks.\n\n**Phase 2: Parallel Processing** (lines 944-966)\n\n```rust\nlet num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n} else {\n    1\n};\n\nlet results: Vec<Round0AirResult> = if num_threads <= 1 {\n    work_items\n        .iter()\n        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w))\n        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?\n} else {\n    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = work_items\n            .chunks(chunk_size)\n            .map(|chunk| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n                    chunk.iter().map(|w| process_air_round0(w)).collect()\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        // Collect from all threads...\n    })?\n};\n```\n\n**Decision Logic:**\n- Single-threaded if < 100 AIRs\n- Multi-threaded if >= 100 AIRs, capped at NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS (8)\n- Each thread processes a chunk of work items sequentially\n\n**Phase 3: Result Scattering** (lines 969-979)\n\n```rust\nlet mut batch_sp_poly = vec![UnivariatePoly::new(vec![]); 3 * num_present_airs];\n\nfor result in results {\n    if let Some(poly) = result.zerocheck_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_numer_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx] = poly;\n    }\n    if let Some(poly) = result.logup_denom_poly {\n        batch_sp_poly[2 * result.trace_idx + 1] = poly;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Storage Pattern:**\n- Indices 0..2*num_present_airs: logup polynomials (2 per AIR: numer, denom)\n- Indices 2*num_present_airs..3*num_present_airs: zerocheck polynomials (1 per AIR)\n\n---\n\n## 5. **Key Data Flow and Computation Patterns**\n\n### Constraint Evaluation Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Source | Round0 Zerocheck | Round0 Logup |\n|-----------|--------|------------------|--------------|\n| skip_domain | l_skip | 1 << l_skip | 1 << l_skip |\n| num_x | n_lift | 1 << n_lift | 1 << n_lift |\n| num_cosets | constraint_degree | deg - 1 | deg |\n| Output size | skip_domain * num_cosets | (1 << l_skip) * (deg-1) | (1 << l_skip) * deg |\n\n### Per-AIR Kernel Launch Pattern (Current)\n\n```\nFor each AIR (sequentially within thread chunk):\n  1. Allocate intermediates buffer\n  2. Allocate temp_sums buffer\n  3. Launch zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints kernel\n  4. Launch logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0 kernel\n  5. Copy outputs to host\n  6. Compute polynomial coefficients (CPU IDFT)\n  7. Free GPU buffers (async)\n```\n\n### Memory Management\n\n- **Intermediate buffer:** Holds DAG node evaluations buffered per row\n  - Size depends on: buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets, max_temp_bytes\n  - Calculated via FFI: `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(...)`\n\n- **Temp sums buffer:** Accumulates polynomial evaluations\n  - For zerocheck: type EF, size calculated via FFI\n  - For logup: type Frac<EF> (2x the size of EF)\n\n- **Per-thread limit:** `memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS`\n  - Allows kernels to allocate adaptively within constraints\n  - Warning logged if actual usage exceeds limit\n\n### Batching Opportunities for Descriptor-Array Implementation\n\n1. **Pre-batching Step:** Group AIRs by compatible parameters\n   - Same constraint_degree → same num_cosets\n   - Same n → same skip_domain, num_x\n   - Batch construction in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` Phase 1\n\n2. **Kernel Launch Pattern:**\n   - Create batch descriptors for all AIRs in each group\n   - Single kernel launch processes all descriptors\n   - Each CUDA block handles one AIR's evaluation\n\n3. **Memory Model:**\n   - Shared intermediates buffer for entire batch (or per-descriptor base pointers)\n   - Shared rules/used_nodes with per-descriptor rule offsets\n   - Per-descriptor output pointers in batch descriptor\n\n4. **Result Collection:**\n   - Batch kernel writes outputs directly to batched buffers\n   - No scatter/gather phase needed\n   - Reduced GPU-CPU synchronization points\n\n---\n\n## 6. **Critical Implementation Details**\n\n### Buffer Size Calculation Philosophy\n\nThe FFI functions return buffer capacities based on:\n- `buffer_size`: DAG nodes needing per-row buffering\n- `skip_domain`, `num_x`, `num_cosets`: Domain size factors\n- `max_temp_bytes`: Maximum allowable GPU memory\n\nThe kernel adapts allocation strategy based on available memory. Allocating more than requested is acceptable (warning only), as kernels handle overallocation gracefully.\n\n### Lambda Powers and Constraints\n\n- `lambda_pows` for zerocheck: powers of lambda for constraint linear combinations\n  - Length = max_num_constraints per AIR\n  - Precomputed before Round 0 phase\n\n- `beta_pows` for logup: powers of beta parameter\n  - Length = max_interaction_length + 1\n  - Shared across all logup evaluations\n\n### Eq_3b Weights (Logup-Specific)\n\n- Computed per AIR based on interaction properties\n- Stored as `eq_3b_per_trace` (Vec<Vec<EF>>)\n- Converted to numer_weights and denom_weights per interaction\n- Weights accumulate when expression nodes are shared\n\n### Polynomial Construction from Evaluations\n\n**Zerocheck:**\n```\n1. Evaluate on cosets indexed by (coset_idx, skip_domain_idx)\n2. Transpose to column-major: values[skip_domain_idx * num_cosets + coset_idx]\n3. IDFT with omega_root (generator of domain)\n4. Compute polynomial coefficients: c_i = -q_i + (i >= skip_domain ? q_{i-skip_domain} : 0)\n```\n\n**Logup:**\n```\n1. Extract (numer, denom) from Frac<EF>\n2. Apply normalization if n < 0\n3. Transpose evaluations\n4. Two IDFTs (numerator and denominator)\n5. Return as separate polynomials\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. **Batching Implementation Recommendations**\n\n### Descriptor Structure\n```rust\npub struct Round0Descriptor {\n    pub air_idx: u32,\n    pub trace_idx: u32,\n    pub n: isize,\n    pub constraint_degree: u32,\n    pub num_cosets: u32,\n    pub skip_domain: u32,\n    pub num_x: u32,\n    pub height: u32,\n    pub output_offset_zc: u32,\n    pub output_offset_logup: u32,\n    pub rules_offset: u32,\n    pub numer_weights_offset: u32,\n    pub denom_weights_offset: u32,\n    // Pointers to shared per-batch data\n}\n```\n\n### Batched Kernel Interface\n```rust\nfn _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched(\n    descriptors: *const Round0Descriptor,\n    num_descriptors: u32,\n    // Shared buffers\n    tmp_sums_buffer: *mut EF,\n    output: *mut EF,\n    selectors_cubes: *const *const F,  // Array of selectors per descriptor\n    // ... other shared inputs\n) -> i32;\n```\n\n### Memory Layout Strategy\n- Allocate single large intermediate buffer with per-descriptor offsets\n- Allocate single large output buffer indexed by descriptor output_offsets\n- Rules and weights concatenated with per-descriptor base offsets\n- Reduces allocation overhead and improves cache locality\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive analysis provides the foundation for understanding how to batch the per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches into descriptor-array based batched kernels."}],"totalDurationMs":79233,"totalTokens":49810,"totalToolUseCount":16,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":42099,"output_tokens":7065,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":644},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7065,"cache_read_input_tokens":42099,"cache_creation_input_tokens":644,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":644,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":12,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
