-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` - Zerocheck constraints\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu` - LogUp interactions\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu` - Batched MLE evaluation pattern\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` - Sumcheck kernels (plain folding)\n\n---\n\n## 1. NttEvalContext and DAG Entry Evaluation (`dag_entry.cuh`)\n\n### `NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS>` Structure\n**Purpose:** Encapsulates all context needed for NTT-based coset evaluation\n**Memory Layout:**\n\n```c\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS> struct NttEvalContext {\n    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed;      // Preprocessed trace data\n    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts;  // Main trace columns (array of pointers)\n    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values;     // Public input values\n    Fp *__restrict__ inter_buffer;            // [buffer_size][NUM_COSETS] per thread\n    Fp *__restrict__ ntt_buffer;              // Shared memory for NTT scratch (NEEDS_SHMEM only)\n    Fp omega_shifts[NUM_COSETS];              // Precomputed: g^((c+1)*ntt_idx_rev) per coset\n    uint32_t skip_domain;                     // 2^l_skip (domain size for NTT)\n    uint32_t height;                          // Trace height\n    uint32_t buffer_stride;                   // Distance between consecutive elements in buffer\n    uint32_t buffer_size;                     // Number of intermediate values\n    uint32_t ntt_idx;                         // Thread's position within skip domain\n};\n```\n\n### Key NTT Evaluation Functions\n\n**`ntt_coset_interpolate<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM, FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY>`**\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\n__device__ __forceinline__ void ntt_coset_interpolate(\n    Fp *__restrict__ results,       // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ evals,   // [height] trace evaluations\n    const Fp *omega_shifts,         // [NUM_COSETS] precomputed shifts\n    Fp *__restrict__ ntt_buffer,    // shared memory scratch\n    uint32_t ntt_idx,\n    uint32_t x_int,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t height,\n    uint8_t offset,\n    bool skip_ntt = false           // Runtime skip flag for identity coset\n);\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n1. Load trace value once: `coeff = evals[(x_int * skip_domain + ntt_idx + offset) & (height - 1)]`\n2. If `skip_ntt` (identity coset in coset-parallel): return coeff directly\n3. If `FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY` (lockstep kernel): store coeff in `results[0]`, skip NTT for coset 0\n4. iNTT once (shared across all cosets): `device_ntt::ntt_natural_to_bitrev<true, NEEDS_SHMEM>`\n5. Save coefficient in register: `saved_coeff`\n6. For each remaining coset c:\n   - Shift: `shifted = saved_coeff * omega_shifts[c]`\n   - Forward NTT: `device_ntt::ntt_bitrev_to_natural<false, NEEDS_SHMEM>(shifted, ...)`\n   - Store: `results[c] = shifted`\n\n**Memory Wrapping:**\n- Uses bitmask: `(base + ntt_idx + offset) & (height - 1)` (height must be power of 2)\n- Allows rotation of trace values across domain\n\n**`ntt_eval_dag_entry<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM, FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY>`**\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\n__device__ __forceinline__ void ntt_eval_dag_entry(\n    Fp *__restrict__ results,        // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    const SourceInfo &src,\n    const NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS> &ctx,\n    const Fp *is_first,              // [NUM_COSETS] per-coset selectors\n    const Fp *is_last,               // [NUM_COSETS] per-coset selectors\n    uint32_t x_int,\n    bool skip_ntt = false            // Runtime flag for identity coset\n);\n```\n\n**Dispatch by entry type:**\n- `ENTRY_PREPROCESSED`, `ENTRY_MAIN`: Call `ntt_coset_interpolate` with column from matrix\n- `ENTRY_PUBLIC`, `SRC_CONSTANT`: Replicate value across all cosets\n- `SRC_INTERMEDIATE`: Load from `inter_buffer[src.index * buffer_stride + c]` (stride=NUM_COSETS in lockstep, 1 in coset-parallel)\n- `SRC_IS_FIRST`, `SRC_IS_LAST`, `SRC_IS_TRANSITION`: Use passed selector arrays\n\n---\n\n## 2. Zerocheck Round 0 (`zerocheck_round0.cu`)\n\n### Constants & Thresholds\n\n```cuda\nconstexpr uint32_t BUFFER_THRESHOLD = 16;          // Switch to global intermediates if buffer_size > 16\nconstexpr uint32_t COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768; // 2^15: use coset-parallel if num_x * skip_domain < this\nconstexpr uint32_t MAX_THREADS = 128;              // Max threads per block\n```\n\n### Device Function: `acc_constraints`\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__device__ __inline__ void acc_constraints(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ constraint_sums,      // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    const NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS> &eval_ctx,\n    const Fp *is_first,                       // [NUM_COSETS] per x_int\n    const Fp *is_last,                        // [NUM_COSETS] per x_int\n    uint32_t x_int,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,  // Lambda scaling factors\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,  // Indices of constraint nodes\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    size_t lambda_len\n);\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n1. Initialize: `constraint_sums[c] = 0` for all cosets\n2. For each rule in DAG:\n   - Decode rule header (op, flags, x operand source)\n   - Evaluate x operand: `ntt_eval_dag_entry<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM>(x_vals, ...)`\n   - Apply operation (ADD, SUB, MUL, NEG, INV, VAR)\n   - If `header.buffer_result` and `buffer_size > 0`: Store in intermediate buffer\n     - **Layout:** `eval_ctx.inter_buffer[z_index * eval_ctx.buffer_stride + c] = x_vals[c]`\n     - **Stride:** `NUM_COSETS` in lockstep mode, `1` in coset-parallel mode\n   - If `header.is_constraint`: Accumulate weighted sum\n     - Consume from `d_used_nodes` and `d_lambda_pows` in order\n     - `constraint_sums[c] += lambda * x_vals[c]`\n\n### Lockstep Kernel: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel`\n\n**Template Parameters:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n```\n\n**Launch Configuration:**\n- **Grid:** `(num_x_blocks, 1)` - NO coset dimension (all cosets handled per thread)\n- **Block:** `(skip_domain * x_per_block)` - Multiple x_int groups per block\n- **Thread Layout (per threadIdx.x):**\n  - `ntt_idx = threadIdx.x & (skip_domain - 1)` (varies fastest)\n  - `x_int_in_block = threadIdx.x >> l_skip`\n\n**Shared Memory Layout:**\n```cuda\nextern __shared__ char smem[];\nFpExt *shared_sum = reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(smem);\nFp *ntt_buffers_base = NEEDS_SHMEM ? \n    reinterpret_cast<Fp *>(smem + blockDim.x * sizeof(FpExt)) : nullptr;\n```\n- `shared_sum[blockDim.x]` for reduction (reused per coset)\n- NTT buffers: `skip_domain` elements per x_int group (only if NEEDS_SHMEM)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,       // [num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ selectors_cube,     // [3][num_x]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed,\n    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_cube,         // [num_x]\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    size_t lambda_len,\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    Fp *__restrict__ d_intermediates,           // Global intermediates buffer\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t height,\n    Fp g_shift\n);\n```\n\n**Key Computation Steps:**\n\n1. **Precompute is_first/is_last multipliers (per coset, once):**\n   - `l_skip = __ffs(skip_domain) - 1`\n   - `ntt_idx_rev = rev_len(ntt_idx, l_skip)` (bit-reversed index)\n   - For each coset c: `g_coset = g_shift^(c+1)`\n   - `eval_point = g_coset * omega_skip_ntt` where `omega_skip_ntt = get_twiddle(l_skip, ntt_idx)`\n   - Segment computation (for is_first/is_last):\n     - `log_segment = min(l_skip, log_height_total)`\n     - `segment_size = 2^log_segment`\n     - `log_stride = l_skip - log_segment`\n     - `omega = exp_power_of_2(eval_point, log_stride)`\n     - `is_first_mult[c] = avg_gp(omega, segment_size)`\n     - `is_last_mult[c] = avg_gp(omega * eta, segment_size)` where `eta = TWO_ADIC_GENERATORS[l_skip - log_stride]`\n\n2. **Intermediate buffer setup:**\n   ```cuda\n   if constexpr (GLOBAL) {\n       // Global mode: Layout [buffer_size][num_threads][NUM_COSETS]\n       inter_buffer = d_intermediates + tidx * NUM_COSETS;\n       buffer_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x * NUM_COSETS;\n   } else {\n       // Local mode: [BUFFER_THRESHOLD][NUM_COSETS]\n       inter_buffer = local_buffer;\n       buffer_stride = NUM_COSETS;\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **Initialize omega_shifts (coset-specific, once per thread):**\n   ```cuda\n   Fp omega_shift_base = pow(g_shift, ntt_idx_rev);\n   for (uint32_t c = 0; c < NUM_COSETS; c++) {\n       eval_ctx.omega_shifts[c] = omega_shift^(c+1)  // Iterative multiplication\n       omega_shift *= omega_shift_base;\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Tile x_int loop:**\n   - `x_int_stride = (gridDim.x * blockDim.x) >> l_skip` (number of x_int values handled in parallel)\n   - `for (x_int = x_int_base; x_int < num_x; x_int += x_int_stride)`\n   - Per iteration: compute is_first/is_last for this x_int\n   - Call `acc_constraints<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM>`\n   - Multiply by eq: `sums[c] += constraint_sums[c] * eq_cube[x_int]`\n\n5. **Reduction (per coset in loop):**\n   ```cuda\n   for (uint32_t c = 0; c < NUM_COSETS; c++) {\n       Fp eval_point = g_coset * omega_skip_ntt;\n       Fp zerofier = exp_power_of_2(eval_point, l_skip) - Fp::one();\n       shared_sum[threadIdx.x] = sums[c] * inv(zerofier);\n       __syncthreads();\n       \n       if (threadIdx.x < skip_domain) {\n           FpExt tile_sum = shared_sum[threadIdx.x];\n           for (uint32_t lane = 1; lane < (blockDim.x >> l_skip); ++lane) {\n               tile_sum += shared_sum[(lane << l_skip) + threadIdx.x];\n           }\n           // Output: [num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]\n           tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * NUM_COSETS * skip_domain + \n                           c * skip_domain + ntt_idx] = tile_sum;\n       }\n       __syncthreads();\n   }\n   ```\n\n### Coset-Parallel Kernel: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel`\n\n**Key Difference from Lockstep:**\n- **Grid:** `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)` - Each (x, coset) pair handled by one block\n- **Coset index:** `coset_idx = blockIdx.y`\n- **NUM_COSETS = 1** always (single coset per block)\n- **Buffer stride:** For global: `gridDim.x * gridDim.y * blockDim.x` (includes num_cosets in layout)\n\n**Precomputation (single coset):**\n```cuda\nFp g_coset = pow(g_shift, coset_idx + 1);\nFp eval_point = g_coset * omega_skip_ntt;\nFp omega = exp_power_of_2(eval_point, log_stride);\nFp is_first_mult = avg_gp(omega, segment_size);\nFp is_last_mult = avg_gp(omega * eta, segment_size);\nFp omega_shift = pow(g_coset, ntt_idx_rev);\n```\n\n**NttEvalContext for single coset:**\n```cuda\nNttEvalContext<1> eval_ctx{\n    ..., {omega_shift}, ... // Single-element omega_shifts array\n};\n```\n\n**Call to acc_constraints:**\n```cuda\nacc_constraints<1, NEEDS_SHMEM>(...);\n```\n\n**Output layout (matches lockstep):**\n```cuda\ntmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * num_cosets * skip_domain + \n                coset_idx * skip_domain + ntt_idx] = tile_sum;\n```\n\n### Final Reduction Kernel: `sumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums`\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <bool ADD_TO_OUTPUT = false>\nstatic __global__ void final_reduce_block_sums(\n    const FpExt *block_sums,    // [num_blocks][d]\n    FpExt *output,              // [d]\n    uint32_t num_blocks\n);\n```\n\n**Launch Configuration (from zerocheck launcher):**\n```cuda\nsumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums<<<NUM_COSETS * skip_domain, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    tmp_sums_buffer, output, num_blocks\n);\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Grid:** `(d,)` where `d = NUM_COSETS * skip_domain` (one block per output)\n- **blockIdx.x** selects which output dimension to reduce\n- Each thread accumulates strided elements: `for (int block_id = tid; block_id < num_blocks; block_id += blockDim.x)`\n- Access pattern: `block_sums[block_id * d + out_idx]`\n- Block-level reduction via `block_reduce_sum(sum, shared)`\n\n---\n\n## 3. LogUp Round 0 (`logup_round0.cu`)\n\n### Device Function: `acc_interactions`\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool NEEDS_SHMEM, bool FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY = false>\n__device__ __inline__ void acc_interactions(\n    const NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS> &eval_ctx,\n    const Fp *is_first,\n    const Fp *is_last,\n    uint32_t x_int,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ numer_weights,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ denom_weights,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    FpExt *__restrict__ numer_sums,            // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    FpExt *__restrict__ denom_sums,            // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    bool skip_ntt = false                      // Runtime flag for identity coset\n);\n```\n\n**Differs from zerocheck:**\n- Produces TWO outputs: numerator and denominator sums\n- Weights are per-node, not via `d_used_nodes` consumption\n- Layout: `numer_sums[NUM_COSETS]`, `denom_sums[NUM_COSETS]`\n\n**Algorithm:**\n1. Initialize both to zero\n2. For each rule:\n   - Evaluate, apply operation (same as zerocheck)\n   - If `buffer_result`: Store intermediate\n   - If `is_constraint`:\n     - `numer_sums[c] += numer_weights[node] * results[c]`\n     - `denom_sums[c] += denom_weights[node] * results[c]`\n\n### Lockstep Kernel: `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel`\n\n**Template Parameters:**\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n```\n\n**Launch Config:** Same as zerocheck (grid.y = 1, no coset dimension)\n\n**Kernel Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,      // [num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]\n    const Fp *__restrict__ selectors_cube,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed,\n    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_cube,\n    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ numer_weights,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ denom_weights,\n    FpExt denom_sum_init,                      // Initial value for denom (per coset)\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    uint32_t buffer_size,\n    Fp *__restrict__ d_intermediates,\n    uint32_t skip_domain,\n    uint32_t num_x,\n    uint32_t height,\n    Fp g_shift\n);\n```\n\n**Key Differences from Zerocheck:**\n\n1. **Omega shift computation (coset 0 is identity):**\n   ```cuda\n   eval_ctx.omega_shifts[0] = Fp::one();  // Identity coset\n   g_coset = g_shift;                     // g^1\n   for (uint32_t c = 1; c < NUM_COSETS; c++) {\n       eval_ctx.omega_shifts[c] = pow(g_coset, ntt_idx_rev);\n       g_coset *= g_shift;\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **acc_interactions call with FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY=true:**\n   ```cuda\n   acc_interactions<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM, /*FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY=*/true>(\n       eval_ctx, is_first, is_last, x_int,\n       numer_weights, denom_weights, d_rules, rules_len, \n       numer_results, denom_results\n   );\n   ```\n\n3. **Accumulation with denom_sum_init:**\n   ```cuda\n   sums[c].p += eq * numer_results[c];\n   sums[c].q += eq * (denom_results[c] + denom_sum_init);\n   ```\n\n4. **Shared memory for FracExt (2 FpExt values):**\n   ```cuda\n   FracExt *shared_sum = reinterpret_cast<FracExt *>(smem);\n   size_t shared_sum_size = sizeof(FracExt) * block.x;\n   ```\n\n5. **Reduction (per coset):**\n   ```cuda\n   for (uint32_t c = 0; c < NUM_COSETS; c++) {\n       shared_sum[threadIdx.x] = sums[c];\n       __syncthreads();\n       \n       if (threadIdx.x < skip_domain) {\n           FracExt tile_sum = shared_sum[threadIdx.x];\n           for (uint32_t lane = 1; lane < (blockDim.x >> l_skip); ++lane) {\n               auto lane_offset = (lane << l_skip) + threadIdx.x;\n               tile_sum.p += shared_sum[lane_offset].p;\n               tile_sum.q += shared_sum[lane_offset].q;\n           }\n           tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * NUM_COSETS * skip_domain + \n                           c * skip_domain + ntt_idx] = tile_sum;\n       }\n       __syncthreads();\n   }\n   ```\n\n### Coset-Parallel Kernel: `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel`\n\n**Grid:** `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)`\n\n**Identity coset detection:**\n```cuda\nuint32_t coset_idx = blockIdx.y;\nbool is_identity_coset = (coset_idx == 0);\n\nFp g_coset = is_identity_coset ? Fp::one() : pow(g_shift, coset_idx);\nFp eval_point = is_identity_coset ? omega_skip_ntt : (g_coset * omega_skip_ntt);\n```\n\n**NTT evaluation (skipping identity):**\n```cuda\nFp omega_shift = is_identity_coset ? Fp::one() : pow(g_coset, ntt_idx_rev);\n\nacc_interactions<1, NEEDS_SHMEM, /*FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY=*/false>(\n    eval_ctx, &is_first, &is_last, x_int,\n    numer_weights, denom_weights, d_rules, rules_len,\n    numer_results, denom_results,\n    is_identity_coset  // skip_ntt flag\n);\n```\n\n### Final Reduction for LogUp\n\n**Key difference:** Uses `2 * NUM_COSETS * skip_domain` as d (because FracExt = 2 FpExt):\n```cuda\nauto large_domain = NUM_COSETS * skip_domain;\nsumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums<<<2 * large_domain, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(tmp_sums_buffer), \n    reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(output), \n    num_blocks\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Batched MLE Pattern (`batch_mle.cu`)\n\n### Context Structures\n\n**`BlockCtx`**\n```cuda\nstruct BlockCtx {\n    uint32_t air_idx;              // Which AIR this block belongs to\n    uint32_t local_block_idx_x;    // Block's x-index within its AIR\n};\n```\n\n**`ZerocheckCtx`**\n```cuda\nstruct ZerocheckCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;          // [preprocessed, main_parts, public_values, selectors]\n    FpExt *d_intermediates;        // Global intermediates [height * buffer_size]\n    uint32_t num_y;                // Y dimension size\n    const FpExt *d_eq_xi;          // [num_y] EQ evaluations (1D folding only)\n    const Rule *d_rules;\n    size_t rules_len;\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes;\n    size_t used_nodes_len;\n    uint32_t buffer_size;\n};\n```\n\n**`LogupCtx`**\n```cuda\nstruct LogupCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n    FpExt *d_intermediates;\n    uint32_t num_y;\n    const FpExt *d_eq_xi;          // [num_y] (1D)\n    const FpExt *d_challenges;     // For ENTRY_CHALLENGE\n    const FpExt *d_eq_3bs;         // [num_interactions] EQ over 3 bits for pair indexing\n    const Rule *d_rules;\n    size_t rules_len;\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes;    // Indices of interaction nodes\n    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs;   // [used_nodes_len] Pair index per used_node: 2*int_idx + is_denom\n    size_t used_nodes_len;\n    uint32_t buffer_size;\n};\n```\n\n### Batched Zerocheck MLE Kernel\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,      // [num_blocks * num_x]\n    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ d_block_ctxs,\n    const ZerocheckCtx *__restrict__ d_zc_ctxs,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n    size_t lambda_len\n);\n```\n\n**Launch Config:**\n- **Grid:** `(num_blocks, num_x)` - One block per (AIR_block, x_int) pair\n- **Block:** `(threads_per_block)` - Threads divided across y dimension\n\n**Algorithm (per thread):**\n```cuda\nuint32_t num_x = gridDim.y;\nuint32_t x_int = blockIdx.y;\nuint32_t y_int = threadIdx.x + block_ctx.local_block_idx_x * blockDim.x;\nbool active_thread = (y_int < zc_ctx.num_y);\n\n// Linear row indexing (no tiling)\nuint32_t height = num_x * zc_ctx.num_y;\nuint32_t row = x_int * zc_ctx.num_y + y_int;\nuint32_t buffer_stride = height;\n\n// Evaluate rules with MLE (no NTT)\nfor (size_t node = 0; node < zc_ctx.rules_len; ++node) {\n    Rule rule = zc_ctx.d_rules[node];\n    FpExt result = evaluate_mle_entry(decoded.x, row, eval_ctx, buffer_stride);\n    // Apply operations, store intermediates\n    // Accumulate constraints via lambda_pows\n}\n\n// Multiply by selector\nsum *= zc_ctx.d_eq_xi[y_int];\n\n// Block reduce\nFpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(sum, shared);\nif (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n    tmp_sums_buffer[blockIdx.x * num_x + x_int] = reduced;\n}\n```\n\n**Key Pattern Differences vs NTT:**\n- NO NTT operations - direct evaluation\n- NO shared memory for twiddles/NTT\n- Row-major iteration (no coset tiling)\n- Simple block reduction using `sumcheck::block_reduce_sum`\n\n### Batched LogUp MLE Kernel\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\n__global__ void logup_batch_mle_kernel(\n    FracExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,\n    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ d_block_ctxs,\n    const LogupCtx *__restrict__ d_logup_ctxs\n);\n```\n\n**Key Algorithm:**\n1. Iterate through `used_nodes_len` in order (alternates: numer, denom, numer, denom, ...)\n2. For each used_node index:\n   - Check if already evaluated (index < rules_evaluated)\n   - If yes: reuse from buffer or OP_VAR value\n   - If no: evaluate all rules up to and including this one\n3. Use `d_pair_idxs[used_idx]` to determine output:\n   - `pair_idx = 2 * interaction_idx + is_denom`\n   - `is_denom = pair_idx & 1`\n4. Accumulate:\n   - `result *= d_eq_3bs[pair_idx >> 1]`\n   - `if (is_denom) denom_sum += result; else numer_sum += result;`\n5. Final scaling: `numer_sum *= d_eq_xi[y_int]`, `denom_sum *= d_eq_xi[y_int]`\n\n### Batched Reduction: `batched_final_reduce_block_sums`\n\n**Signature:**\n```cuda\nstatic __global__ void batched_final_reduce_block_sums(\n    const FpExt *block_sums,           // [total_blocks][d]\n    FpExt *output,                     // [num_segments][d]\n    const uint32_t *segment_offsets,   // [num_segments + 1]\n    uint32_t d\n);\n```\n\n**Launch Config:**\n```cuda\n// From _zerocheck_batch_eval_mle:\ndim3 reduce_grid(num_airs, num_x);\nsumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums<<<reduce_grid, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    tmp_sums_buffer, output, air_block_offsets, num_x\n);\n\n// From _logup_batch_eval_mle (FracExt = 2 FpExt):\ndim3 reduce_grid(num_airs, 2 * num_x);\nsumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums<<<reduce_grid, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(tmp_sums_buffer),\n    reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(output),\n    air_block_offsets,\n    2 * num_x\n);\n```\n\n**Algorithm:**\n- **Grid:** `(num_segments, d)`\n- **blockIdx.x (seg_idx):** Which segment (AIR)\n- **blockIdx.y (out_idx):** Which output dimension\n- **Lookup segment bounds:** `start = segment_offsets[seg_idx]`, `end = segment_offsets[seg_idx+1]`\n- **Strided accumulation:** `for (uint32_t i = tid; i < num_blocks; i += blockDim.x)`\n- **Access:** `block_sums[(start + i) * d + out_idx]`\n- **Block reduce and write:** `output[seg_idx * d + out_idx] = sum`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Reduction Kernel Details (`sumcheck.cuh`)\n\n### `block_reduce_sum(FpExt val, FpExt *shared)`\n\n**Two-stage process:**\n1. **Warp-level reduction:** `warp_reduce_sum(val)` via `__shfl_down_sync`\n2. **Inter-warp via shared memory:**\n   - Lane 0 of each warp writes to `shared[warp_id]`\n   - First warp (warp_id == 0) reduces all warp results\n   - Returns result available in all threads of first warp\n\n### `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` Details\n\n**Memory access pattern:**\n- Input: `block_sums[total_blocks][d]` (row-major by block)\n- Output: `output[num_segments][d]`\n- Each (seg, out_idx) block reduces blocks `[segment_offsets[seg]...segment_offsets[seg+1])`\n\n**Shared memory:**\n```cuda\nextern __shared__ char smem[];\nFpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n// Size calculated as: max(1u, reduce_warps) * sizeof(FpExt)\n// where reduce_warps = (block.x + 31) / 32\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Coset-Parallel vs Lockstep Mode Decision\n\n**Dispatcher function:**\n```cuda\ninline bool use_coset_parallel_mode(uint32_t num_x, uint32_t skip_domain) {\n    return (num_x * skip_domain) < COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD;\n}\n// COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768 (2^15)\n```\n\n**When to use coset-parallel (grid.y = num_cosets):**\n- Small workload: `num_x * skip_domain < 32768`\n- Better GPU utilization: each coset gets its own set of blocks\n- Trade-off: Slightly more block overhead, but better occupancy for small problems\n\n**When to use lockstep (grid.y = 1):**\n- Larger workload: `num_x * skip_domain >= 32768`\n- Single thread handles all cosets\n- Advantage: iNTT done once, reused across all cosets\n- Twiddle factor cost is amortized over NUM_COSETS\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table: Kernel Signatures\n\n| Kernel | Mode | Grid | Block | Input | Output |\n|--------|------|------|-------|-------|--------|\n| `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel<NUM_COSETS, GLOBAL, NEEDS_SHMEM>` | Lockstep | `(num_x_blocks, 1)` | `(skip_domain * x_per_block)` | selectors, rules, eq_cube | `tmp_sums_buffer[num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]` |\n| `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel<GLOBAL, NEEDS_SHMEM>` | Coset-parallel | `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)` | `(skip_domain * x_per_block)` | (same) | (same layout) |\n| `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel<NUM_COSETS, GLOBAL, NEEDS_SHMEM>` | Lockstep | `(num_x_blocks, 1)` | `(skip_domain * x_per_block)` | numer_weights, denom_weights, denom_sum_init | `tmp_sums_buffer[num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]` as FracExt |\n| `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel<GLOBAL, NEEDS_SHMEM>` | Coset-parallel | `(num_x_blocks, num_cosets)` | (same) | (same) | (same layout) |\n| `zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel` | Batched | `(num_blocks, num_x)` | `(threads_per_block)` | rules, lambda_pows, eq_xi | `tmp_sums_buffer[num_blocks * num_x]` |\n| `logup_batch_mle_kernel` | Batched | `(num_blocks, num_x)` | (same) | rules, numer/denom, pair_idxs, eq_3bs | `tmp_sums_buffer[num_blocks * num_x]` as FracExt |\n| `final_reduce_block_sums<ADD_TO_OUTPUT>` | Reduction | `(d,)` | `(reduce_block)` | block_sums[num_blocks][d] | output[d] |\n| `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` | Batched reduction | `(num_segments, d)` | `(reduce_block)` | block_sums[total_blocks][d] | output[num_segments][d] |\n\n---\n\n## Memory Layout Summary\n\n**NTT Mode (Round 0 kernels):**\n- `tmp_sums_buffer`: `[num_blocks][NUM_COSETS * skip_domain]` (row-major)\n- `inter_buffer` (global): `[buffer_size][num_threads][NUM_COSETS]` (lockstep) or `[buffer_size][num_cosets * num_threads]` (coset-parallel)\n- `inter_buffer` (local): `[buffer_size][NUM_COSETS]` per thread\n\n**MLE Batched Mode:**\n- `tmp_sums_buffer`: `[num_blocks * num_x]` (flattened for zerocheck, FracExt for logup)\n- `output`: `[num_blocks * num_x]` (or via batched reduction to `[num_airs][num_x]`)\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive summary should give you all the details needed to write batched versions. The key patterns to follow are:\n1. Grid/block configuration and thread indexing\n2. Shared memory layout (especially for NTT vs reduction)\n3. Intermediate buffer stride computation\n4. Accumulation patterns (constraint sums, interaction sums with weights)\n5. Block reduction followed by final multi-block reduction"}],"totalDurationMs":80923,"totalTokens":66438,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14502,"cache_read_input_tokens":41949,"output_tokens":9980,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14502},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":9980,"cache_read_input_tokens":41949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14502,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":8,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"li